WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.984
Structured outputs on Claude today.

2
00:00:02.264 --> 00:00:04.291
Claude offers two related features.

3
00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:09.797
JSON outputs constrain the response itself: you pass a schema in output_config.

4
00:00:10.077 --> 00:00:15.197
format with type json_schema, and the reply’s text block is JSON matching it.

5
00:00:15.477 --> 00:00:23.477
Strict tool use constrains tool arguments: you add strict: true to a tool definition, and calls to that tool always validate.

6
00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.677
You can use both in one request.

7
00:00:25.957 --> 00:00:32.464
The older top-level output_format request parameter is deprecated; the current home is output_config.

8
00:00:32.744 --> 00:00:33.512
format.

9
00:00:33.792 --> 00:00:36.416
In Python, the recommended path is client.

10
00:00:36.696 --> 00:00:37.613
messages.

11
00:00:37.893 --> 00:00:38.704
parse().

12
00:00:38.984 --> 00:00:48.776
You pass your Pydantic class (the SDK’s parse() helper takes it as output_format ), the SDK converts it to a schema and sends it as output_config.

13
00:00:49.056 --> 00:00:53.451
format, and the response carries a validated instance in parsed_output.

14
00:00:53.731 --> 00:01:10.179
The SDK also adapts the schema: the API supports a subset of JSON Schema, and the docs list what’s out, including recursive schemas, numeric bounds such as minimum, string length bounds such as minLength, and any additionalProperties other than false.

15
00:01:10.459 --> 00:01:19.291
The SDK helpers move unsupported constraints into the field description and then check your original constraints when they validate the response.

16
00:01:19.571 --> 00:01:23.496
That’s another reason to keep the Pydantic model as your source of truth.

17
00:01:23.776 --> 00:01:26.144
Some operational details from the docs.

18
00:01:26.424 --> 00:01:34.872
The first request with a new schema pays a one-time compilation cost; compiled grammars are cached for 24 hours from last use.

19
00:01:35.152 --> 00:01:39.291
Changing the format invalidates the prompt cache for that conversation.

20
00:01:39.571 --> 00:01:42.643
Structured outputs can’t be combined with citations.

21
00:01:42.923 --> 00:01:54.208
And the guarantee has stated exceptions: if stop_reason is refusal or max_tokens, the output may not match the schema, so check the stop reason before you trust parsed_output.
